# Line-ending policy.
#
# The Windows host runs with `core.autocrlf=true`. Without this file Git would
# rewrite the working tree to CRLF, and CRLF is what reaches the Linux dev
# container over the /mnt/d bind mount. That breaks shell shebangs
# (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` -> "bad interpreter") and other text tooling. Force LF
# in the working tree for every text file. Keep this minimal: it is a policy for
# future checkouts, not a bulk renormalisation of the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must always be LF, with no exceptions.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never convert, never diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.parquet binary
*.xlsx binary
*.heapsnapshot binary
